hold('D75','Source D combines caring about people’s problems and affairs, which overlap. The Arabic saying concerns opposing the oppressor and helping the oppressed; the source’s text layout and broad options do not support a precise single-best answer.');
hold('D76','Source B is not a blanket immunity rule. Competence, precaution, valid permission or release conditions, causation of harm and the applicable religious/legal framework must be distinguished. A patient accepting risk does not automatically eliminate every responsibility.');
hold('D77','Source A depends on switching the meaning of Islam from common submission to the final dispensation, while B also ambiguously uses “brothers.” Distinguish biological kinship from other uses and the common core from historical dispensations. No unique scored key.');
hold('D78','Source A describes resurrection, not the full ascension chronology. The New Testament distinguishes the third-day resurrection from the forty-day period in Acts before ascension. Preserve the original conflation with this correction.');
hold('D79','Source C attributes the proposal to Shaytan, but the visitor, approver and proposer roles have not been independently resolved in the exact report. Dar al-Nadwah is a meeting place, not a person.');
scored('D80','D','Thawr is the migration refuge in the reviewed narrative. Hira belongs to the retreat/first-revelation setting, not this escape.','This is not the refuge named in the migration account.','Dar al-Nadwah is the council setting, not the migration cave.','Najaf is not the cave identified in this narrative.');
scored('D81','A','The course’s Thaqalayn formulation names the Quran and Ahl al-Bayt as the two weighty things.','This is not the pair in the reviewed formulation.','This substitutes the Prophet for Ahl al-Bayt in the pair asked for.','A cow is not an element of the course’s Thaqalayn formulation.');
hold('D82','Source D combines struggles and differences but names no event or sufficiently bounded historical claim. Study the review’s succession/authority framework; do not invent a particular episode to repair the vague source stem.');
hold('D83','Source A names Thaqalayn, the two weighty things, but the stem repeats the typo “demise of holy quran.” The intended event is the Prophet’s demise. Correct teaching is Quran plus Ahl al-Bayt; original wording remains visible.');
scored('D84','B','Dar al-Nadwah is the meeting setting in the reviewed Quraysh narrative. It is distinct from the migration refuge Thawr.','Najd is not the council venue named here.','Thawr is the refuge, not the meeting venue.','The venue is listed in B.');
hold('D85','Source B reports that the old visitor was Satan. Preserve this as a traditional narrative attribution; the exact report and transmission status have not been authenticated in the available review.');
scored('D86','A','The invitation to near relatives is associated with Yawm al-dar in the reviewed narrative. Distinguish it from Dar al-Nadwah.','Yawm al-adha is not the event name used for this invitation.','The reviewed event name is available in A.','A and a denial of every option cannot both be correct here.');
hold('D87','Source C names Muhammad ibn Jarir al-Tabari as a compiler of the narrative. The precise passage has not been established in the review, and a later compiler must not be treated as an eyewitness.');
hold('D88','Source B is the paper’s simplified truth-pluralist definition. Actual religious pluralist theories do not all assert identical truth or value of every claim. Learn which model is being discussed, rather than treating the broad wording as universally descriptive.');
hold('D89','Source C expresses freedom of religious choice. That is a tolerance/liberty claim, not by itself a distinctive proof or definition of religious pluralism. Do not collapse treatment of persons with truth or salvation.');
hold('D90','Source B describes salvation across religions, but its wording can be read as a guarantee for all followers. Cross-tradition possibility and guaranteed salvation of every person are different claims.');
scored('D91','A','The intended distinction is that people can differ in degree or strength of faith. This does not imply unequal human dignity or authorize contempt.','The account explicitly allows degrees of faith.','Membership in a religious group does not erase differences in commitment.','The variation intended by the stem is represented in A.');
hold('D92','Source D gives ten degrees like a ladder, attributed to the sixth Imam. The exact narration and chain remain unauthenticated here; do not use it to supply the unnamed three stages of D19.');
hold('D93','Source B records the highest-rank claim for the Prophet and his household. The exact attributed report remains unverified; moral or spiritual ranking must not become a denial of anyone’s dignity.');
hold('D94','Source C combines garbled options about one revealed religion. The stable course teaching is shared foundational guidance with different applicable laws. The exact wording is too unclear for a forced combined key.');
hold('D95','Source C combines statements whose meanings conflict unless time and the sense of “true” are qualified. Earlier missions’ original truth differs from the continuing applicability of every earlier law. The original does not supply those distinctions.');
hold('D96','Source C confuses contradiction between doctrinal propositions with the fate of individuals. The review treats doctrinal truth, freedom and salvation separately; individual judgment also involves access and responsibility.');
scored('D97','A','Divine unity is the fundamental belief intended. This is not a claim that a complete account of Islam contains no other beliefs or prescriptions.','Imamah is important in the Twelver framework but is not the shared foundational unity asked for.','This adds a particular authority-and-conduct formulation rather than isolating the main belief.','Prayer is a practical obligation added to the belief; A identifies the foundation directly.');
hold('D98','The sheet chooses D, but C and D are effectively duplicate objections. Their broad dismissal also fails to identify a specific pluralist theory or argument. The review teaches the distinctions rather than force-scoring the original.');
scored('D99','D','The item intends the noncompulsion principle of Quran 2:256. A truth claim and rejection of coercion are distinct; noncompulsion does not mean every practice is arbitrary.','This contradicts the noncompulsion principle asked for.','Noncompulsion is not an unrestricted claim that every way of practice is equivalent.','This does not state the noncompulsion principle.');
scored('D100','D','The original embedded verse is Quran 3:85. In the course interpretation it concerns acceptance of religion, not a license to force belief. Keep it distinct from Quran 2:256 and from judgments about particular people’s access or culpability.','This is not the acceptance statement expressed by the supplied verse in the course interpretation.','Personal preference is not the criterion expressed by the verse.','A claim about acceptance does not itself authorize coercion.');

scored('A3','C','Positive attributes affirm a perfection; negative attributes deny a deficiency. These are distinct classifications, not good versus bad attributes of God.','Positive is a usable technical classification in this account.','Affirmation of perfection and denial of deficiency are not identical forms of predication.','The definition of positive attributes is supplied in C.');
scored('A4','A','The course rejects blanket judgments about all followers of other religions. Individual circumstances, adequate access and capacity matter; this is not a verdict about a named person.','This imposes universal condemnation without the qualifications discussed.','This imposes universal guaranteed salvation without the qualifications discussed.','The reviewed material does discuss these distinctions.');
scored('A5','B','The course describes one revealed core of submission to God while locating differences among missions in practical prescriptions. This is its framework, not an assertion of identical doctrines everywhere.','This erases the course’s distinction between earlier and final applicable dispensations.','Conduct matters, but the technical definition does not dispense with beliefs.','The course does not ground revealed guidance simply in national preference.');
hold('A6','The paper intends A, but Paraclete does not lexically mean Muhammad. It belongs to helper/advocate/comforter terminology; John 14:26 identifies the Holy Spirit. A Muslim prophetic interpretation is a separate claim. The source has no fully accurate lexical answer.');
scored('A7','C','In the reviewed non-bodily account, divine hearing and seeing refer to knowledge rather than physical ears and eyes.','This introduces bodily organs contrary to the account.','The terms are used with a non-bodily interpretation, not prohibited outright.','Power is a different perfection from the knowledge expressed here.');
scored('A8','B','The number of adherents does not by itself establish that a religion’s claims are true. Proposed rationality, preservation or prediction criteria still require their own evidence.','The course treats rational assessability as relevant rather than mere head count.','Preservation is among the criteria discussed, though it alone is not sufficient proof.','A prediction claim can be assessed textually; it must not simply be assumed.');
scored('A9','D','In the reviewed migration narrative Ali sleeps in Muhammad’s bed while Muhammad leaves.','Abu Bakr has a different role in the migration account.','Umar is not assigned the bed role in this narrative.','Uthman is not assigned the bed role in this narrative.');
scored('A11','B','CORRECTED from the source’s highlighted D. The broad definition is putting things in their proper place. Allocation according to relevant capacity can be an application, not the complete definition.','Identical shares need not respect relevant entitlements or differences.','Avoiding oppression is related, but does not give the specific positive definition asked for.','This describes a possible allocation principle rather than the general definition.');
scored('A12','A','The course’s unity argument connects guidance with a shared human nature. This is a premise within its theological account, not a claim that every historical doctrine is identical.','The assertion that Abraham is father of all prophets is not the stated nature-based argument.','A general appeal to following Adam does not give the stated reasoning about shared nature.','The shared-nature premise is supplied in A.');
hold('A14','The intended A mixes a supported identification of Maurice Bucaille as a French physician/writer with an unverified conversion claim. No complete option is safely scored as written. His arguments and personal religious biography must be evaluated separately.');
scored('A15','C','Honoring parents appears both in the Decalogue and in Quranic teaching, such as Quran 17:23. Both statements fit the requested comparison.','This is true but omits the Quranic counterpart.','This is true but omits the Decalogue counterpart.','Both sources contain the teaching, so none is incorrect.');
hold('A17','The intended C joins the temporary/enduring contrast with a claim about changing destiny. In the review, this life is the opportunity for choice and cultivation; that must not imply revision of God’s complete knowledge. Because B uses unqualified “destiny,” the original is retained with explanation rather than force-scored.');
scored('A19','B','The question’s “three principles” means broad contents: beliefs, practical orders and moral values. Do not confuse this with the separate three shared doctrinal fundamentals.','Fasting is an example of a practical obligation, not a third broad area alongside practice.','Honesty is a moral example, so this duplicates rather than completes the content classification.','Numbered placeholders do not identify the three content areas.');
hold('A20','The original highlights B, psychological function. The review preserves that intended classification for making life meaningful, while distinguishing explanatory/noetic functions and acknowledging overlap. The unqualified wording does not warrant silently replacing B with A or claiming the distinction is absolute.');

// Aligned against the original O-paper's actual option order, not reconstructed distractors.
